1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,600
At 06:00, five hundred guests are coming.

2
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:07,000
The Valio cut-off is 10:00. One wrong guess can stop service.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,500
The chef decides.

4
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:13,100
One photo becomes a checked request.

5
00:00:13,100 --> 00:00:15,800
Facts, permission, and the chef's hand stay visible.

6
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:18,500
Read, check, hold, approve.

7
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:23,500
This is one continuous take. I photograph a Finnish kitchen list.

8
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:31,000
Gemini reads the handwritten Finnish list.

9
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:39,000
Live Valio price, stock, delivery date, and pack size.

10
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:47,000
Voice: change the potatoes to 30 kilograms.

11
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:55,000
The cart is held over the EUR 1,500 limit.

12
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:02,000
The chef taps Approve. The agent still cannot approve.

13
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Ordered, signed, and tied to the build.

14
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:20,500
One take. No speed-ups. The reasoning stays visible.

15
00:01:20,500 --> 00:01:24,800
Gemini returns a yes-probability for every assumption.

16
00:01:24,800 --> 00:01:29,000
Above 0.70 it acts. Below it asks.

17
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:33,200
Codex built this engine with parallel workers.

18
00:01:33,200 --> 00:01:37,500
Forty-two main commits say Built by Codex. 787 tests pass.

19
00:01:37,500 --> 00:01:42,000
CRACI runs all seven CI jobs and publishes the build evidence.

20
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:46,000
351 components, 17 destinations. Every order names its build.

21
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:49,000
The order is confirmed.

22
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:55,000
Agents knock. The door checks. The chef decides.
